  "response_complete": true,
  "response_text": "The following are some of the warning signs of alcohol withdrawal:\n\n  1. Seizures: This is the most serious and life-threatening symptom of alcohol withdrawal. Seizures can occur within hours of stopping alcohol use and can be life-threatening.\n  2. Delirium Tremens (DTs): This is a severe and potentially life-threatening condition that can occur in some people who stop drinking alcohol suddenly. Symptoms of DTs include confusion, hallucinations, and tremors.\n  3. Hallucinations: Some people who stop drinking alcohol suddenly may experience hallucinations, which are false perceptions or sensations that seem real but are not based in reality.\n  4. Severe anxiety or panic attacks: Some people who stop drinking alcohol suddenly may experience severe anxiety or panic attacks.\n  5. Severe depression: Some people who stop drinking alcohol suddenly may experience severe depression.\n  6. Severe fatigue: Some people who stop drinking alcohol suddenly may experience severe fatigue.\n  7. Severe tremors: Some people who stop drinking alcohol suddenly may experience severe tremors.\n  8. Severe sweating: Some people who stop drinking alcohol suddenly may experience severe sweating.\n  9. Severe diarrhea: Some people who stop drinking alcohol suddenly may experience severe diarrhea.\n  10. Severe headache: Some people who stop drinking alcohol suddenly may experience severe headache.",
